 ;; --- (a) AArch64 UEFI loader spike -----------------------------------------
 :aarch64-uefi-loader
 {:status :boots-under-real-uefi
  :artifact "BOOTAA64.EFI, PE32+ executable (EFI application) Aarch64, 4608 bytes"
  :build ["clang --target=aarch64-unknown-windows -ffreestanding -fshort-wchar -fno-stack-protector -O1 -c"
          "lld-link -subsystem:efi_application -entry:efi_main -nodefaultlib"]
  :qemu-exit 0
  :serial-markers
  ["AIUEOS_AARCH64_UEFI_ENTRY"
   "AIUEOS_UEFI_REVISION 0x0000000000020046"
   "AIUEOS_GOP_OK base=0x0000000000000000 size=0 w=1280 h=800 stride=1280 format=3"
   "AIUEOS_MEMMAP_OK entries=32 descsize=48"
   "AIUEOS_EXIT_BOOT_SERVICES_OK"
   "AIUEOS_CURRENT_EL 1"
   "AIUEOS_AARCH64_UEFI_OK"]
  :negative-control
  {:invocation "--expect-fail (FAT32 ESP with no EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI)"
   :result "all 6 required markers absent; gate rejects"
   :note "The gate was watched failing before being recorded as landed."}
  :findings
  [{:finding :calling-convention
    :detail "AArch64 UEFI uses the platform AAPCS64 default, so EFIAPI is empty.
             The x86_64 loader's __attribute__((ms_abi)) on every protocol
             function pointer is the single largest source-level difference."}
   {:finding :no-port-io
    :detail "AArch64 has no port I/O at all. The x86_64 evidence path (COM1 at
             0x3f8) becomes PL011 MMIO at 0x09000000 on QEMU virt."}
   {:finding :termination
    :detail "isa-debug-exit (x86_64, iobase 0xf4) has no AArch64 counterpart.
             PSCI SYSTEM_OFF (0x84000008 via HVC #0) terminates QEMU with exit 0
             and is the deterministic replacement."}
   {:finding :exception-level
    :detail "AAVMF hands control at EL1 on machine virt (CurrentEL >> 2 = 1),
             not EL2. A kernel wanting EL2 must be entered before firmware or
             re-enter deliberately."}]}

 ;; --- The load-bearing display finding: this is what couples (a) and (c) ----
 :aarch64-gop-display-matrix
 {:machine "qemu-system-aarch64 -machine virt, AAVMF"
  :why "The x86_64 desktop-surface bootstrap takes the GOP LINEAR APERTURE
        (framebuffer_base/size), maps it RW+NX uncached, and presents a
        retained-rectangle test frame with a readback hash. That bootstrap only
        ports to a device that actually exposes an aperture."
  :efi-pixel-format {0 :PixelRedGreenBlueReserved8BitPerColor
                     1 :PixelBlueGreenRedReserved8BitPerColor
                     2 :PixelBitMask
                     3 :PixelBltOnly}
  :devices
  [{:device "virtio-gpu-pci"
    :gop :present
    :pixel-format 3
    :pixel-format-name :PixelBltOnly
    :framebuffer-base "0x0000000000000000"
    :framebuffer-size 0
    :resolution [1280 800]
    :linear-aperture? false
    :note "The idiomatic AArch64 display device gives Blt-only GOP with NO
           aperture. The x86_64 desktop-surface bootstrap does not port to it."}
   {:device "ramfb"
    :gop :present
    :pixel-format 1
    :pixel-format-name :PixelBlueGreenRedReserved8BitPerColor
    :framebuffer-base "0x000000005c7a0000"
    :framebuffer-size 3145728
    :resolution [800 600]
    :stride 800
    :linear-aperture? true
    :note "The only probed AArch64 device exposing a real linear aperture."}
   {:device "VGA"           :gop :absent :linear-aperture? false
    :note "AAVMF binds no GOP; there is no CSM/VGA BIOS execution on ARM.
           vgabios-stdvga.bin was present, so this is not a missing-rom artifact."}
   {:device "bochs-display" :gop :absent :linear-aperture? false
    :note "Same as VGA: rom present, no GOP bound."}
   {:device "virtio-vga"    :gop :not-applicable :linear-aperture? false
    :note "'virtio-vga' is not a valid device model name on aarch64 — it is
           x86-only because it bundles VGA compatibility. This is exactly the
           device os/aiueos/scripts/smoke-qemu-uefi.sh uses on x86_64, so the
           existing smoke gate's display device does not exist on AArch64."}]
  :consequence
  "AArch64 desktop parity requires either (i) ramfb for the early surface, or
   (ii) the virtio-gpu 2D resource path (create resource, attach backing,
   transfer, flush) that os/aiueos/README.md currently lists as intentionally
   excluded. Therefore virtio-gpu 2D moves from 'Phase 6, later' to 'required
   for AArch64 desktop', and tracks (a) and (c) are coupled rather than
   independent."}

 ;; --- What this evidence does NOT show -------------------------------------
 :not-demonstrated
 ["A kernel. The spike is a UEFI loader; it does not yet hand off to an
   aarch64 KERNEL.ELF, so nothing below ExitBootServices is exercised."
  "Any desktop. No compositor, no widget tree, no input path; the GOP numbers
   are a capability probe, not a rendered surface."
  "Anything on macOS. No Mac host in this session, so HVF, the
   com.apple.security.hypervisor entitlement, and Apple Silicon virtio-gpu
   behaviour are all unmeasured."
  "Real hardware. ramfb's aperture and its 800x600 mode are QEMU artifacts;
   Apple Silicon exposes neither ramfb nor this GOP shape."]}
